@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] contracts-never-weakened
A contract MUST NOT be deleted, loosened or reworded to make code pass. When behaviour
changes on purpose, the contract changes in the same pull request, and its prose says
which decision changed it. A known violation is named in the pull request that finds it
until the code is fixed. "All these things that I've been saying over all these videos
have to be in contracts ... so we do not make the same mistakes" (recording 15 Oct 13:54,
07:13; K15).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] contracts-cite-their-source
A contract written from Tavi's feedback MUST name where it came from in its prose: the
recording and the time, the point (F, H, J or K numbers of the design notes) or the
`android/DESIGN.md` rule. A contract with no traceable source is a guess and is not added.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] contracts-live-by-their-code
A rule about one directory's code MUST live in the `CONTRACTS` file of that directory (or
the nearest one above it); Kotlin and Vue rules always go in a `CONTRACTS` file, since
`cc-check` does not read those languages. Every `CONTRACTS` file MUST pass
`pnpm run contracts:check`: a directive per contract, an `owner` and a `label` on each,
non-empty prose, and an ID used once in its file and in every `CONTRACTS` file above it.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] contracts-readable-in-app
Every `CONTRACTS` file in the repository MUST reach the Android app at build time and be
listed on the UI Book's Contracts page, sorted by area, with nothing left out or edited
by hand. Adding a `CONTRACTS` file needs no other change for it to show there
(message 15 Oct, "a section under the UI book for code contracts").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] phone-api-one-account
The phone's API (`POST /api/rpc` and `GET /android/*`) stays behind Cloudflare Access with
the headers the phone is given in Settings, as before. The server has one account, seeded
from the environment, with no sign-up and no GitHub connection; the phone signs in to it
with email and password once and stays signed in until Sign out. The account's own
methods (its keys, synced settings and posted diffs) MUST need that session; the rest of
the phone API is reached as before. This replaces "no login" by Tavi's decision of 16 Oct
12:40 and 12:47 (plan "Posted diffs"). Google sign-in MAY come later.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] agent-api-needs-a-key
`/api/v1/*` is the only part of the server meant to sit outside Cloudflare Access, and it
MUST answer 401 to every call without a valid account key. A key reaches only its own
account's posted diffs: no phone method, no GitHub token, no AI run, no other account
(Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47: "that endpoint doesn't really allow them to do anything unless they
pass a valid API key").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] posted-diffs-not-on-the-web
A diff an agent posted opens only in the phone app, signed in to the account. The web page
MUST NOT read one: the web RPC refuses a `posted:` target or key and hides a posted diff's
stored records and cache entries, and `/-/<id>` on the web only says to open it in the app
(Tavi, 16 Oct 14:17: "just block access for everyone. On the web, I mean. And I mean
specifically for these new agent diffs").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] account-secrets-kept-as-hashes
The server keeps the account's password only as a salted PBKDF2 hash, and its sessions and
API keys only as SHA-256 hashes. A key is shown once, when it is made; afterwards only its
name and first letters are shown. None of them MAY be written into an answer, an error, a
log line or a usage event.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] github-token-stays-on-server
The GitHub token is resolved on the server and used only there. It MUST NOT be sent to
the phone or the page, written into an answer, an error, a log, an AI prompt or a work
log, or be readable through any method the phone may call.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] secrets-come-from-the-environment
Keys for paid services (TypeSafe, the Pi endpoint, model providers) come only from the
server's environment. A client names an engine and a model, never a URL or a key, and no
answer, notice or log line MAY echo a key or any part of it.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] one-look-two-clients
The web app and the phone app are one product with one look (DESIGN.md rule 106). Colours,
type, radii, shadows, icons and fonts are defined once, in the front matter of
`android/DESIGN.md`, `Lu` in `Icons.kt` and `PullsFonts`, and carried to the web by
`pnpm run android:design:update`; neither side MAY add a value of its own.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] strings-from-web-locales
The phone's strings come from the web's locale files: `android/app/src/main/assets/i18n`
MUST equal `packages/app/src/i18n/locales` byte for byte (DESIGN.md Enforcement, web). A
string is added once, at the web's locale, and copied over.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] agents-act-through-pr-tools
An AI job reads and acts on a pull request through the server's own tools (the PR tools
over MCP, `piTools` for Pi). It MUST NOT be given a writable checkout, the server's own
files, the user's skills or a shell beyond its job folder, "so that they can't really
like mess anything up" (recording 14 Oct 19:19, 01:10 to 01:35).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] analyses-run-side-by-side
Two analyses of different pull requests MUST be able to run at the same time. No analysis
switches the branch of a checkout another job reads, and the server MUST NOT make a fresh
clone of the repository for every run (recording 14 Oct 19:19, 00:29 to 01:05).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] analytics-stays-on-our-server
Usage analytics from the phone, the web app and the server go only to our own server,
which keeps them as one NDJSON file per UTC day in its own folder. No analytics, crash or
telemetry package or third-party service MAY be added for it (message 15 Oct 20:58, "We
will track them directly on our server. No need for fancy packages").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] analytics-what-not-how-much
Analytics records what was done, never what was read or typed: no token or key, no diff,
file contents, file path, prompt, AI answer, comment, Ask message or search text. Events
carry counts, timings, enums, on or off values and a pull request's repo and number, and
`cleanEvent` in `packages/core/src/analytics.ts` enforces it on the server before any
event is written (plan "Pulls analytics on our own server", Guardrails).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] analytics-can-be-turned-off
Each client has a Usage stats switch in Settings, on by default; turning it off drops
what is queued and sends nothing more. `PULLS_REVIEW_ANALYTICS=off` on the server stops it
writing anything, its own events included. Day files older than 365 days are deleted
(plan "Pulls analytics on our own server", Guardrails).
